From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: cdns-dphy: set up the PSM divider in power_on

cdns_dphy_setup_psm() programs the divider of the power state machine
clock. Our driver called it from cdns_dphy_configure(); mainline calls it
from cdns_dphy_power_on(), after enabling the clocks, and set_psm_div is
part of the generic reference ops, so this is not J721E specific.

Move it. power_on becomes self-sufficient for the state machine it
starts, which fits the is_configured / is_powered guard model, and the
divider is programmed while psm_clk is enabled, the clock that power_off
now gates. If setup fails, the three clocks just enabled are released.

Of all the changes in this series this is the one that alters the order
in which PHY registers are programmed: the PSM divider is now written
after the clock lane, PLL and band configuration instead of before them,
though still before the state machine is started. If behaviour gets
worse after this series, this is the first patch to take out.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
@@ -287,14 +287,6 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	/*
-	 * Configure the internal PSM clk divider so that the DPHY has a
-	 * 1MHz clk (or something close).
-	 */
-	ret = cdns_dphy_setup_psm(dphy);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	/*
 	 * Configure attach clk lanes to data lanes: the DPHY has 2 clk lanes
 	 * and 8 data lanes, each clk lane can be attache different set of
 	 * data lanes. The 2 groups are named 'left' and 'right', so here we
@@ -325,6 +317,7 @@
 {
 	struct cdns_dphy *dphy = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
 	u32 reg;
+	int ret;
 
 	if (!dphy->is_configured || dphy->is_powered)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -333,6 +326,15 @@
 	clk_prepare_enable(dphy->pll_ref_clk);
 	clk_prepare_enable(dphy->esc_clk);
 
+	/* PSM clock divider for a ~1 MHz state machine clock. */
+	ret = cdns_dphy_setup_psm(dphy);
+	if (ret) {
+		clk_disable_unprepare(dphy->esc_clk);
+		clk_disable_unprepare(dphy->pll_ref_clk);
+		clk_disable_unprepare(dphy->psm_clk);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	/* Start TX state machine. */
 	reg = readl(dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
 	writel((reg & DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME) | DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN | DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN,
